Z||000000||turbo86se||09-16-2001||10:01 PM||||I downloaded the PIP into the C drive, I think, where it went from there I'm lost. How do I unzip it? Where do I go now? What do I do?  <BR>I've been web-tv handicapped for so long, now I've got a sweet PC with scanner. <BR>HELP!<BR>I'm lost!<BR>Thanks!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||09-16-2001||10:49 PM||||You will need some sort of program to unzip with, unless it has become self-extracting since the last time I down loaded and installed it. I can't remember where on the web you can get a copy of winzip free, but there are several places. anyway, you need to download winzip, then use it to install PIP in its own directory. Mine is in c:/prog/pip. I used ctrl panel-install new software to do it, that way if something goes awry, you can uninstall it and try it again. It is pretty much fail-proof tho. Even Don was able to do it and he is dumber than dirt.<BR>Email me if you have any trouble. I've got a set of instructions for using PIP once it is installed. The instructions in the manual are pretty straightforward tho.||||reg||1
